  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.helsinki.fi/job/Helsinki-POSTDOCTORAL-OR-DOCTORAL-RESEARCHER-IN-PHOTOCATALYTIC-RADICAL-CHEMISTRY/1373062857/": {
      "title": "POSTDOCTORAL OR DOCTORAL RESEARCHER IN PHOTOCATALYTIC RADICAL CHEMISTRY",
      "description": "POSTDOCTORAL OR DOCTORAL RESEARCHER IN PHOTOCATALYTIC RADICAL CHEMISTRY Job Details | University of Helsinki We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login VIEW ALL JOBS VIEW BY CATEGORY Professors, assistant and associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions CAREERS Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login Search by title, unit or a word Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » POSTDOCTORAL OR DOCTORAL RESEARCHER IN PHOTOCATALYTIC RADICAL CHEMISTRY The University of Helsinki, Department of Chemistry, invites applications for a postdoctoral or doctoral researcher position in photocatalytic radical chemistry at the newly established Lahdenperä Group. Initially, the position is fixed-term for 12-months with a possibility of an extension. Position description The successful candidate will join an organic chemistry research group at the Department of Chemistry located at Kumpula campus. The research group aims to develop new concepts for controlling radical reactivity in photocatalytic transformations. The project focuses on the development of new approaches for controlling radical reactivity through hydrogen atom transfer (HAT) at surfaces and interfaces. Highlights of PI’s previous work on photochemistry: Science (2024): Chiral hydrogen atom abstraction catalysts for the enantioselective epimerization of meso diols. JACS (2025): Catalytic deracemization of 1,2-aminoalcohols through enantioselective hydrogen atom abstraction. JACS (2022): Enantioselective Giese additions of prochiral α-amino radicals, establishing new methods for asymmetric radical C-C bond formation. The project will involve: Development and optimisation of photocatalytic radical transformations Mechanistic studies of radical reactions and detailed investigation of HAT processes. Surface functionalization and interface chemistry. Design and synthesis of organic molecules. The postdoctoral researcher will additionally be expected to contribute to the supervision of students and participate in future funding applications. Requirements Postdoctoral Researcher Applicants must hold a PhD degree in chemistry or a closely related field by the start of employment, or be close to completion of their doctoral studies. Consideration will be given to candidates with experience in one or more of the following areas: synthetic organic chemistry. photocatalysis, radical chemistry, hydrogen atom transfer processes. reaction mechanism studies. flow chemistry. The successful candidate should demonstrate the ability to conduct independent research and publish scientific results in international peer-reviewed journals. Doctoral Researcher Applicants must hold a Master's degree (or equivalent) in chemistry or a closely related discipline that qualifies them for doctoral studies at the University of Helsinki. Previous experience in organic synthesis, photochemistry, catalysis or related experimental chemistry is advantageous but not required. Selected candidates for the interview process will be required to provide a copy of their university transcript before interview date. For both positions We are looking for candidates who are: highly motivated and scientifically curious. willing to develop new experimental skills. persistent and independent in tackling challenging research questions. Excellent written and oral communication skills in English are required. Salary and benefits The salary follows the salary system of University salary system and is based on the researcher's qualifications, experience, and stage of doctoral or postdoctoral career. For postdoctoral researchers, the starting salary will be approximately 3900–4200 €/month. For doctoral researcher the starting salary will be approximately 2600–2800 €/month. University of Helsinki offers comprehensive services to its employees, including occupational health care, sports facilities, and ample opportunities for professional development and language studies. The International Staff Services office ( https://www.helsinki.fi/en/university/working-at-the-university ) assists employees from abroad with their transition to work and life in Finland. A diverse and equitable study and work culture is important to the University of Helsinki. That is why we do our best to promote an inclusive university community. We encourage all qualified applicants from different gender identities, linguistic and cultural backgrounds, and minorities to apply for the position. You can read about the accessibility and inclusivity of our university via this link. How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum vitae, including a publication list (if applicable). A concise motivation letter describing your research interests, relevant experience, reasons for applying and career plans. Please indicate your desired starting date in the application. Degree certificate (PhD for postdoctoral applicants; Master's degree for doctoral researcher applicants). If you are interviewed, you will be asked for contact details for two references. The deadline for applications is October 16th, 2026. Ideally, the selected candidate will start as soon as possible, although flexibility in the starting date can be arranged. Regardless, candidates who are unable to start immediately are still encouraged to apply. The selected applicants will be given support to apply for available grants or fellowships. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a suitable candidate is found. Interviews may start before closing date 16.10.2026 . Additional information Further information about the position can be obtained from Dr. Antti Lahdenperä, antti.sk.lahdenpera@helsinki.fi . For questions regarding the recruitment system please contact: recruitment@helsinki.fi . Do you have a helsinki.fi username and a valid employment contract, a grant researcher's contract, a visiting researcher's or visiting professor's contract at the University of Helsinki? Log in here to apply to our open positions. Employee Login Open position Due Date: 16.10.2026 (23.59 Europe/Helsinki time) Unit: Faculty of Science Sub-unit: Department of Chemistry ID: 5230 Working for the world Science has the power to change the world. Join one of the best research universities in the world – an international community united through bold thinking, science, research, and learning, with over 30,000 students and 8,000 employees. We are defined by our multidisciplinary approach. This, combined with a dedication for cross-border collaboration, gives us our potential to find real solutions and build hope for a better, more sustainable future. We are united by our values – truth, bildung, freedom, and inclusivity – as well as our passion for work that truly matters. Join us: work for the future – work for the world. Any questions? See our recruitment system FAQ Apply now » Find similar jobs: Teaching and research positions Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CONTACT Data protection Contact us WHY US? Why University of Helsinki Why Finland CAREER SITES Academic careers Expert careers FACULTIES AND UNITS Flamma intranet Faculties and Units © University of Helsinki 2022 × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled Google Tag Manager Google Tag Manager is a tag management system for conversion tracking, site analytics, remarketing and more. Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider GoogleTa