    "https://jobs.helsinki.fi/job/Helsinki-Director-of-Communications-and-Community-Relations/1373466857/": {
      "title": "Director of Communications and Community Relations",
      "description": "Director of Communications and Community Relations Job Details | University of Helsinki We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login VIEW ALL JOBS VIEW BY CATEGORY Professors, assistant and associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions CAREERS Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login Search by title, unit or a word Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Director of Communications and Community Relations The University of Helsinki is seeking a DIRECTOR OF COMMUNICATIONS AND COMMUNITY RELATIONS to lead and develop the University’s Communications and Community Relations sector and serve as a strategic partner to the University’s senior leadership. About the position The director of communications and community relations serves as a strategic partner to the rector, vice-rectors and other members of the University leadership in matters relating to communications, advocacy and community relations. You will lead the University’s Communications and Community Relations sector and ensure that its activities support the University’s strategic plan, enhance the University’s international profile and promote the societal impact of research. You will oversee a sector of more than 100 specialists and be responsible for goal-oriented development. The Communications and Community Relations sector’s remit covers communications about strategic projects, the University brand, media relations, marketing, public engagement, alumni activities, fundraising, activities of the Think Corner venue and the organisation of major events at the University. You will be a member of the University Services management group and report to the director of administration. This is a permanent position starting on 1 January 2027 or as agreed. What kind of leader are we looking for? We are looking for an experienced and visionary leader with the ability to lead communications and community relations comprehensively in line with strategic objectives. You understand how research-based knowledge, public debate and policy-making are interconnected. You actively follow changes in the operating environment and anticipate their impact on the University of Helsinki. You use data, analytics and research knowledge to support decision-making. You understand the impact of technology and artificial intelligence on communications and continuously develop your expertise and that of the organisation. You interact naturally with audiences ranging from the University community to the media, policy-makers and other stakeholders in society. You know how to strengthen the global visibility of the University and research. To succeed in this position, you must have: Strong experience of leading and strategically developing communications, community relations and advocacy work The ability to set a clear long-term course of action and the determination to implement it The ability to communicate difficult issues clearly and convincingly Experience with crisis communications A goal-oriented and enhancement-led approach to leadership An excellent understanding of society, decision-making and the media environment A master’s or equivalent degree from a relevant field In our culturally diverse organisation and in international collaboration, you will need excellent Finnish as well as fluent English and Swedish. Why choose the University of Helsinki? At the University of Helsinki, you will work in an environment where research, education and society come together. In this position, you will contribute to how the University communicates about its research and teaching, participates in public debate and promotes the role of research in society. We offer you a meaningful and wide-ranging leadership position at Finland’s most internationally renowned university, including the opportunity to work with a highly skilled and motivated community of specialists. The University is guided by the values of truth, Bildung, freedom and inclusivity. Interested? Please submit your motivation letter, CV and salary expectation by 19 October 2026 through the University of Helsinki recruitment system. The recruitment process is carried out in cooperation with JFP Executive Search Oy. For further information about the position, please primarily contact JFP Executive Search’s Markku Leskinen (markku.leskinen@jfp.fi, tel. +358 500 637 003). The supervising manager, Administrative Director Esa Hämäläinen, is also available upon request (tel. +358 29 412 2212, admindirector@helsinki.fi). Do you have a helsinki.fi username and a valid employment contract, a grant researcher's contract, a visiting researcher's or visiting professor's contract at the University of Helsinki? Log in here to apply to our open positions. Employee Login Open position Due Date: 19.10.2026 (23.59 Europe/Helsinki time) Unit: University Services Sub-unit: Communications and Community Relations ID: 5234 Working for the world Science has the power to change the world. Join one of the best research universities in the world – an international community united through bold thinking, science, research, and learning, with over 30,000 students and 8,000 employees. We are defined by our multidisciplinary approach. This, combined with a dedication for cross-border collaboration, gives us our potential to find real solutions and build hope for a better, more sustainable future. We are united by our values – truth, bildung, freedom, and inclusivity – as well as our passion for work that truly matters. Join us: work for the future – work for the world. Any questions? See our recruitment system FAQ Apply now » Find similar jobs: Leadership specialist and support positions Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CONTACT Data protection Contact us WHY US? Why University of Helsinki Why Finland CAREER SITES Academic careers Expert careers FACULTIES AND UNITS Flamma intranet Faculties and Units © University of Helsinki 2022 × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled Google Tag Manager Google Tag Manager is a tag management system for conversion tracking, site analytics, remarketing and more. Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider GoogleTagManager Google Analytics Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider GoogleAnalytics LinkedIn LinkedIn is an employment-oriented social networking service. We use the Apply with LinkedIn feature to allow you to apply for jobs using your LinkedIn profile. Opting out of LinkedIn cookies will disable your ability to use Apply with LinkedIn. Cookie Policy Cookie Table Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider LinkedIn Confirm My Choices Accept All Cookies"
